{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For near is the day of their calamity, and hastening things to come upon them, when HaShem judges His people.</b> For truly the day of the nations' calamity will be near, when HaShem judges His people, as it says: וּבָרוֹתִי מִכֶּם הַמּוֹרְדִים וְהַפּוֹשְׁעִים (Ezekiel 20:38), for then the remaining nations will quickly perish." "<b>And for His servants He will have compassion.</b> He will relent from the evil decreed upon His people and have compassion on them for the sake of His servants who are among them, as it says: כֵּן אֶעֱשֶׂה לְמַעַן עֲבָדַי לְבִלְתִּי הַשְׁחִית הַכֹּל (Isaiah 65:8)." "<b>For He sees that power is gone.</b> The reason He will then relent from the evil decreed upon His people, and that He will do so for the sake of His servants — and did not do so all the days of exile — is that then He sees Israel at the very depths of the affliction and pressure of exile, such that they can no longer survive in it, as was the situation in Egypt, as it says: וַיַּרְא אֶת עָנְיֵנוּ וְאֶת עֲמָלֵנוּ וְאֶת לַחֲצֵנוּ (Deuteronomy 26:7)." "<b>And none shut up or left outside.</b> He will see that they no longer have wealth stored up in the house or left in the field."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:22.501060025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}